55,3,1,talk,Servas,,"Looking at the candidates, Ledger Bridge seems the most promising. It is a pure software solution for financial reconciliation, avoiding the physical appraisals and staffing nightmares we discussed.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,3,1,talk,Asuka,,"I agree. Ledger Bridge avoids the physical infrastructure that led to our write-off and, unlike the medical or field-based options, it aligns with our most profitable exit profiles.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,3,1,talk,Minako,,Ledger Bridge is the safest bet for our reserves. It avoids the hardware costs and staffing drains that would otherwise accelerate our capital depletion.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,3,1,talk,Mio,,"Ledger Bridge sounds perfect! It's software, so it won't need those hard-to-find field crews, and it doesn't seem like it would overwhelm our already busy software partners.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,3,1,talk,Toshio,,"I concur. It avoids the security delays associated with medical records and the supply chain risks of hardware, making it the most efficient choice for our current constraints.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,2,talk,Servas,,I see no reason to hesitate. The alignment here is absolute; Ledger Bridge is the only candidate that respects both our time and our treasury.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"It is the most logical choice. The other candidates—Clinic Scheduler, Harvest Sensor, and Fabric Loop—all introduce the exact operational and regulatory risks we have agreed to avoid.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,2,talk,Minako,,I agree. Ledger Bridge provides the stability we need without the risk of unexpected capital calls or restrictive credit limitations.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,2,talk,Mio,,I'm all in for Ledger Bridge! It's definitely the one that won't make us all stressed out with hiring or board meetings!,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,2,talk,Toshio,,I agree. It is the only option that minimizes the risk of deployment delays and avoids the bottlenecks we've identified.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,3,talk,Servas,,"Since we are in complete agreement, I believe we can move directly to the vote to finalize this decision.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,3,talk,Asuka,,I agree. There is no further need for deliberation when the evidence and our collective concerns point so clearly to one candidate.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,3,talk,Minako,,I concur. Let us proceed to the vote and secure this investment.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,3,talk,Mio,,I'm ready! Let's make it official and pick Ledger Bridge!,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
